# =============================================================================
# .gitignore
#
# The repository contains code only. Everything the pipeline reads from the
# restricted HILDA release, and everything run_all.R generates, stays out of
# version control. A fresh clone reproduces all of it: synthetic panels are
# rebuilt from a fixed seed by 00b_make_synthetic_hilda.R, and tables and
# figures are rebuilt by the pipeline.
# =============================================================================

# ── Data: restricted (real) and generated (synthetic) panels ──────────────────
# All analysis panels are .rds and are either confidential or regenerated, so
# none are committed. This covers both the real panels written by
# 00_load_hilda.R and the synthetic ones written by 00b_make_synthetic_hilda.R,
# whether they land in the repo root or under data/.
*.rds
data/raw/
data/analysis/
data/synthetic/

# Keep the placeholder READMEs that explain those folders, if present.
!data/raw/README.md
!data/analysis/README.md

# ── Derived result tables ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Several stages write result ledgers and summary tables (se_ledger_*.csv,
# robustness_master.csv, event_study_beta2.csv, dial_*.csv, and others) by bare
# name into the working directory. They are regenerated by the pipeline, so they
# are not committed. The repository has no committed .csv inputs; if you ever add
# one, force-add it with `git add -f` or add a negation below.
*.csv

# ── Generated outputs and run logs ────────────────────────────────────────────
output/
run_logs/
figures/          # legacy local figures dir; current runs use output/figures/

# ── R session and project cruft ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Renviron

# ── Editor and OS files ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
~$*               # Office lock files (Word style guide, decks)
*.RData
tableA3_estimator_note.txt
